Find the greater \(x\)-value of the real solutions to the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
y &= 2x^2 \\
y &= x^2 + 4x
\end{align*}

Find the greater \(x\)-value of the real solutions to the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
y &= x^2 \\
y &= 2x^2 - 3x
\end{align*}

Find the greater \(x\)-value of the real solutions to the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
y &= 3x^2 \\
y &= 2x^2 + 5x
\end{align*}

Find the greater \(x\)-value of the real solutions to the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
y &= 3x^2 \\
y &= x^2 + 4x
\end{align*}

Find the greater \(x\)-value of the real solutions to the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
y &= x^2 \\
y &= 3x^2 + 4x
\end{align*}

Find the greater \(x\)-value of the real solutions to the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
2x^2 - y &= x - 2 \\
x^2 + y &= 2x + 8
\end{align*}

Find the greater \(x\)-value of the real solutions to the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
y &= (x - 2)^2 - 7 \\
y &= -x^2 + 4x + 21
\end{align*}

Find the greater \(x\)-value of the real solutions to the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
y &= x^2 - 2x + 3 \\
y &= 2x^2 - 5x - 1
\end{align*}

Find the greater \(x\)-value of the real solutions to the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
y &= 3x^2 - 4x - 1 \\
y &= x^2 + 3x - 4
\end{align*}

Find the greater \(x\)-value of the real solutions to the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
x^2 - x - y &= -2 \\
2x^2 - 4x - y &= 8
\end{align*}
